# Docker reads this file from the build-context root, not from the Containerfile's directory —
# a copy under `deploy/container/` would never be consulted. The build context is `server/` alone,
# so this is the file that decides what the image carries.
#
# What is excluded and why:
#   node_modules  the image installs its own from the lockfile; a copied tree would bake in the
#                 developer's platform and any local patch.
#   data          the database, attachments, and backups are a host volume, never image content.
#   *.sqlite*     a stray database file committed by accident must not ship.
#   .env          secrets never enter an image layer; the deployment passes them at run time.
#   tests         the suite is a development artifact. Keeping it out also keeps the image from
#                 advertising test fixtures and expected secrets to anyone who can pull it.
node_modules
data
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
.env
tests
